Launcher @LAUNCHER_DISPLAY_VERSION@ - Windows 10 and 11, x64
@LAUNCHER_RELEASE_STATUS@

@LAUNCHER_LICENSE_NOTICE@
Included third-party components retain their own licenses; see
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.

Extract all files. Beside the Launcher-R@LAUNCHER_DISPLAY_VERSION@-windows-x64
folder are Install.cmd for setup and Portable.txt for extract-and-run directions.
You can also run Launcher Setup.exe from inside that folder.
For portable use, open that versioned folder and run
Launcher-R@LAUNCHER_DISPLAY_VERSION@.exe. Keep that folder's contents together.
Setup preserves your settings
and offers optional sign-in startup; see docs\Installer.html. A fresh installation
offers Program Files or a personal installation without administrator approval.
Hover over the tabs to reveal the panel. Click a tab to switch pages, and click
an icon with a configured target to launch it. Right-click a tab or blank area
for Edit configuration, Open configuration folder, Adjust sizes, About, and Quit.
About shows the executable's version, build time, commit ID and build type;
Copy details copies these for a report.

Portable use first looks for Launcher.toml beside the running EXE, then in
%LOCALAPPDATA%\Długosz\Launcher. Installed use looks in that AppData folder.
Runtime adjustments stay beside the selected configuration with its basename.
The bundled Launcher.default.toml seeds a missing portable configuration.
Setup uses Launcher.installed.default.toml to prepare a missing AppData
Launcher.toml after handling any portable profile, and seeds its personal color
demo as Demos\demo_many_colors.toml before launch and its icon under Icons.
It preserves existing demo edits and
runtime settings. Upgrades update exact stock guide/demo links in an existing
Launcher.toml with a backup; unrelated text and custom entries are preserved.
If an installed copy later cannot find it, Launcher shows a modal creation/exit
prompt. Portable first use creates its missing adjacent configuration quietly.
Fresh setup can transfer root TOMLs and files under Icon or Icons into AppData.
Upgrade setup warns about differing trial files and does not copy them. See
docs\Installer.html for transfer details and existing-profile protection.

For a separate portable trial when AppData already holds another profile, copy
Launcher.default.toml to Launcher.toml beside the versioned EXE before starting.
Otherwise the AppData profile is used when no adjacent Launcher.toml exists.
Edit Launcher.toml, then choose Restart. Keep relative icon files beneath Icon
or Icons so setup can transfer them coherently on a fresh installation.
For repair, retained-version selection and removal, see docs\Installer.html.
Installed copies appear as Długosz Launcher in Programs and Features / Installed
apps. Choose Uninstall there, or use the included Uninstall.cmd with the exact
installation directory. Portable use creates no Windows uninstall entry.

The starter tabs open the included Launcher tools and guides, standard Windows
apps, and the shipped examples. Open docs\Launcher.html for the main guide.
HTML guides open in your browser and work offline. The main guide links to
the detailed configuration, launch targets, and appearance references. Open
the editable TOML examples in Notepad.

Basic and extra colors are embedded in the running EXE as basic_colors.toml and
extra_colors.toml. Those fixed files and colors-light.toml/colors-dark.toml are
also supplied in the examples subdirectory for browsing and copying. That
directory is not searched at runtime. Copy a fixed file into your
settings folder under its original name to load it automatically. Or copy any
supplied file as colors-custom.toml, edit it, and select colors = "custom".
Only selectable sets use colors-<name>.toml, such as colors-light.toml.
Later files replace matching names; partial = true changes only supplied fields.
Color names use ASCII, normalized to lowercase. Restart to apply palette edits.
Use Try the many-colors demo on the Examples tab to see all 21 colors on a wide top-edge
dock. Its demo_many_colors.toml selects light; change colors to "dark" to compare.

An item can be written as: { label = "Notepad", target = "notepad.exe" }
Omit icon to use the target's icon, or specify an icon override. GUI and console
programs, shortcuts, documents, folders, and links use Windows Shell launching.
Console programs are visible by default. Icon-only items remain placeholders.
Quit and restart Launcher to apply edits to the configuration.

LauncherDrop.exe is a small companion for building configuration entries. Drop
programs, documents, folders, or shortcuts onto its top zone, repeat as needed,
then Copy All. Open Launcher.toml using its dedicated Notepad button or the
Other editors dropdown below it, and paste the entries
inside the desired tab's items = [ ... ] list. The helper generates text only;
save your edits in your editor, then quit and restart Launcher to apply them.

LauncherSvgExtractor.exe is the included companion for finding SVG artwork in
programs and installation folders. Run it when needed, choose a source and a
results folder, then browse its gallery. Keep copies an image into your personal
Launcher Icons folder; put the saved filename in an item's icon field.
It uses .NET Framework 4.6.2 or later. Setup installs it alongside Launcher;
no separate installation is needed. See docs\SvgExtractor.html for instructions.

Odd minor versions denote development after the preceding even release series.
Even minor versions identify release series, including release candidates.

